Hut
The interior of the hut is cramped and gloomy. Thick soot cakes the solitary
window, leaving the flickering flames of a stone hearth as the room's sole
source of light. Atop the fire, rusted iron vessels bubble quietly, venting
strange, multi-coloured vapours. A massive, cluttered workbench is buried under
a chaotic heap of heavy grimoires, brittle sheets of paper, and exotic
alchemical ingredients. A heavy wooden door leads north, back out to the forest
path.

Resting within a small alcove in the stone wall is a beautifully carved, gilded
wooden box.

Your old mentor, Istar, is hunched over the workbench, intently poring over a
faded tome. When he sees you he says, "My boy, I am so glad to see you again.
Great tasks await us, but to begin with, I need you to read this." He picks up a
slim, leather-bound folio and presses it into your hands. "It is the culmination
of everything I have uncovered since my exile."

> i
